# Line endings.
#
# Git's `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites text files to CRLF
# on checkout. A CRLF `solve.sh` or `test.sh` cannot be executed inside the
# Linux container harbor runs: bash reads `#!/bin/bash\r` as a request for an
# interpreter named `bash\r`, the oracle exits 127, the verifier never runs and
# no reward.txt is written. See harbor/TROUBLESHOOTING.md.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf

# The harbor example asserts the sha256 of its input CSV, so the working-tree
# bytes have to match on every platform.
*.csv text eol=lf
